# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# xtask's fixture scratch. Named `target/` but not a cargo build dir: xtask
# tests write throwaway workspaces and codegen `.rmeta` outputs under it. It
# was unignored, so 104 of those outputs were once committed by accident and
# then orphaned when the fixtures moved to per-run mkdtemp leaves.
/xtask/target/

# Fetched / generated inputs — recreate with `cargo xtask`
/vendor/
/.cache/

# Downloaded tooling (trunk et al) — recreate with scripts/
/.tooling/

# Scratch capture workspace — not part of the build
/.capture/

# Deletion-drill scratch (see plan §3.2); recreate with `cargo xtask check-deletable`
/.deletion-drill-backup/

# Debug artifacts from headless/window render runs — regenerate on demand,
# never commit. These are outputs of tests, not inputs to them.
/*.png
/*.ppm
/*.log

# Decompiled reference source: NEVER commit (Mojang-copyrighted)
**/mc/*/src/
**/mc/*/client-src/
*.jar

# Benchmark measurement data (docs/benchmark-regression-gate.md) — local dev
# artifacts, not comparable across machines, never committed.
/bench-results/

# A vanilla server booted in the repo root writes here (oracle/JVM dump runs).
# Never repo state.
/logs/

# rustc ICE dumps. Written into whatever directory rustc was invoked from, so
# they land in the repo root and are untracked where another agent's `git add`
# can sweep them up. Four appeared in one minute from a single incremental-cache
# fingerprint failure -- they are diagnostic scratch, never repo state.
rustc-ice-*.txt

# OS
.DS_Store

# stray per-run logs from live gates
**/.session_*.log
lodestone-frame.ppm
*.ppm
